          %title
          %p This entry provides some hyperlinks for the articles
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+S.+Freed"}> Daniel S. Freed
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %em> Loop Groups and Twisted K-Theory I
                    ,
                  %p J. Topology, 4 (2011), 737-789
                  %p
                    (
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0711.1906"}> arXiv:0711.1906
                    ,
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/jtopol/jtr019"} doi:10.1112/jtopol/jtr019
                %li#PartII
                  %p
                    %em> Loop Groups and Twisted K-Theory II
                    ,
                  %p J. Amer. Math. Soc. 26 (2013), 595-644
                  %p
                    (
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0511232"}> arXiv:0511232
                    ,
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0894-0347-2013-00761-4"} doi:10.1090/S0894-0347-2013-00761-4
                %li
                  %p
                    %em> Loop Groups and Twisted K-Theory III
                    ,
                  %p Annals of Mathematics, Volume 174 (2011) 947-1007
                  %p
                    (
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0312155"}> arXiv:math/0312155
                    ,
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.4007/annals.2011.174.2.5"} doi:10.4007/annals.2011.174.2.5
          %p
            about the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+ad-equivariant+K-theory"} twisted ad-equivariant K-theory
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+energy+representations"} positive energy representations
            of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+groups"} loop groups
            (forming the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verlinde+ring"} Verlinde ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+induction"} Dirac induction
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+method"} orbit method
            for producing representations by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+orbits"} coadjoint orbits
          %p Exposition:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+S.+Freed"}> Daniel S. Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Verlinde algebra is twisted equivariant K-theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0101038"} arXiv:math/0101038
          %p
            This identification enhanced to an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+S.+Freed"}> Daniel S. Freed
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %p
                %em> Dirac families for loop groups as matrix factorizations
                ,
              %p Comptes Rendus Mathematique, Volume 353, Issue 5, May 2015, Pages 415-419
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1409.6051"}> arxiv/1409.6051
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.crma.2015.02.011"} doi:10.1016/j.crma.2015.02.011
          %blockquote
            %p
              We identify the category of integrable lowest-weight representations of the loop group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L G
              of a compact Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              with the linear category of twisted, conjugation-equivariant curved Fredholm complexes on the group
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+factorizations"} matrix factorizations
              of a super-potential built from the loop rotation action on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L G
          %h2#statement_of_the_theorem Statement of the theorem
          %p
            Every
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+valued+differential+form"} valued differential form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Omega^1(S^1, \mathfrak{g})
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            defines an element in the free
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group"} loop group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            on a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            over the circle.
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+bundle"} spinor bundle
            over the circle, and using a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group+representation"} loop group representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            one can hence shift its defining connection by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and form the associated Dirac operator
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_A
          %p
            By remembering for each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hol
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hol(A) \in G
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+operators"} Fredholm operators
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            This construction is (
            %a{:href => "#PartII"}> FHT, part II, cor. 3.39
            ).
          %p
            The FHT-theorem asserts that this construction gives an equivalence of the category of loop group representations at some level
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verlinde+ring"}> Verlinde ring
            ) and the
            = succeed "-" do
